WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.834 --> 00:00:11.546
Diego Alvarez: Hey Cody, hey Hector. Thanks for making time this afternoon.

2
00:00:12.746 --> 00:00:21.125
Cody Barrett: Hey Diego. Good to see you. Hector's joining because a chunk of what we want to talk about touches the Spanish floor.

3
00:00:22.166 --> 00:00:28.580
Hector Ruiz: Hola Diego. I'm on a headset in the bullpen, so if it gets loud you'll know why.

4
00:00:28.981 --> 00:00:33.681
Diego Alvarez: No problem at all. Before we get into it, how's volume looking this month?

5
00:00:34.361 --> 00:00:43.698
Cody Barrett: We're tracking around 9,400 calls for September across the three states. Texas is still the biggest, Arizona's been creeping up since the Phoenix push.

6
00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:49.196
Diego Alvarez: That's up from the low eights last time we talked, right?

7
00:00:50.142 --> 00:00:55.088
Cody Barrett: Yeah, maybe eight percent. Meta's been doing more of the work lately, Google's roughly flat.

8
00:00:55.949 --> 00:01:04.549
Hector Ruiz: Spanish calls are about a third of that. We finally got the second bilingual pod fully staffed, so hold times are way down from the summer.

9
00:01:06.017 --> 00:01:12.518
Diego Alvarez: Good timing heading into Q4. Anything you want me to look at while we're on?

10
00:01:13.492 --> 00:01:25.749
Cody Barrett: One thing, and it's the main reason I asked for this session. The offline conversions we send to Google Ads are landing one to three days after the call.

11
00:01:25.749 --> 00:01:32.090
Cody Barrett: Not all of them, but enough that Smart Bidding is optimizing on a partial picture.

12
00:01:33.524 --> 00:01:37.923
Diego Alvarez: Okay. Is it consistent across campaigns, or worse on some?

13
00:01:38.186 --> 00:01:45.920
Cody Barrett: Worse on the residential campaigns with the longer sales cycle. Some conversions show up same day, others drag out two or three days.

14
00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:50.291
Cody Barrett: We can't tell what's a slow sync and what's just a slow sale.

15
00:01:51.006 --> 00:01:59.222
Hector Ruiz: And the Spanish campaigns are in that same bucket. Those leads take longer to close, so they're probably hit hardest.

16
00:01:59.431 --> 00:02:02.092
Diego Alvarez: Got it. When did you first notice it?

17
00:02:02.947 --> 00:02:12.253
Cody Barrett: About three weeks ago. I pulled a report for our Monday standup and the numbers didn't line up with Salesforce, so I started digging.

18
00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:15.571
Diego Alvarez: And what's the impact on bidding right now?

19
00:02:16.759 --> 00:02:27.009
Cody Barrett: We moved one campaign, the Austin residential one, to manual bidding as a stopgap. I didn't want the algorithm making decisions on data that's still trickling in.

20
00:02:27.519 --> 00:02:30.226
Diego Alvarez: How long has that one been on manual?

21
00:02:30.785 --> 00:02:38.287
Cody Barrett: Since last Thursday. It's fine for now, but I don't want to run the whole account that way through the winter.

22
00:02:39.152 --> 00:02:50.399
Diego Alvarez: Understood. I'll need a couple of examples, campaign names and a few call IDs where the timing was off, so I can take it to the team with something concrete.

23
00:02:50.945 --> 00:02:55.091
Cody Barrett: I can send those tonight. I already have a spreadsheet going.

24
00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.923
Diego Alvarez: Perfect. Anything else on the integration side?

25
00:03:00.124 --> 00:03:03.274
Cody Barrett: Salesforce and Meta are fine. No complaints there.

26
00:03:03.532 --> 00:03:12.192
Hector Ruiz: From the floor, everything else is working. Signal AI is tagging our Spanish calls well enough that the leads route correctly.

27
00:03:13.469 --> 00:03:23.396
Diego Alvarez: Good. Let me get the examples over to the team, and I'll come back to you with next steps. I don't want to guess at what's happening until they've looked.

28
00:03:23.747 --> 00:03:25.460
Cody Barrett: That's all I'm asking.

29
00:03:26.529 --> 00:03:38.158
Diego Alvarez: One more thing while I have you. Renewal's on the calendar for the end of November. Do you want to do a quick business review before then, or keep it simple?

30
00:03:39.639 --> 00:03:48.400
Cody Barrett: Let's do a short one. Thirty minutes, just the three of us. I'll get Hector's numbers for the bilingual side.

31
00:03:49.772 --> 00:03:53.803
Hector Ruiz: I can pull those by the second week of October.

32
00:03:55.220 --> 00:04:00.452
Diego Alvarez: Great. I'll send a couple of times for the week of the twelfth.

33
00:04:01.574 --> 00:04:10.354
Cody Barrett: Works for me. And hey, if the team needs anything else from us, just say so. I'd rather over-share than have them chasing ghosts.

34
00:04:10.995 --> 00:04:15.183
Diego Alvarez: Appreciate that. I'll follow up after I hear back. Thanks, both.

35
00:04:16.465 --> 00:04:18.565
Hector Ruiz: Thanks Diego. Back to the phones.

36
00:04:19.945 --> 00:04:20.745
Cody Barrett: Talk soon.
